The '''Axis network safehouse''' was an apartment on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]] was used by [[Luthen Rael]]'s [[Axis network]]. It was located on [[Level 5124]], Plate seven grid, 3561 East.<ref name="Kyber">{{Andor|Jedha, Kyber, Erso}}</ref> A secure high-rise apartment, the safehouse was used by rebels to lay low while in between missions. The safehouse had a kitchen, which included large windows allowing for a panoramic view of the Coruscant skyline, a bedroom, and a dining area. The space was overall sparse and bare and at times dark and dingy.<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|axis-network-safehouse|Axis Network safehouse}}</ref> Rael stayed in the safehouse on two occasions. In [[3 BBY]], the rebels [[Cassian Jeron Andor]] and [[Bix Caleen]] used the safehouse.<ref name="Ever Been" />

[[File:Axis network safehouse main.jpg|thumb|300px|left|Bix and Cassian sit for a meal at the safehouse table.]]
In [[2 BBY]], [[Senator]] [[Mon Mothma]] was taken to the safehouse to hide after her [[escape from the Senate]] following her public speech condemning [[Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine]] for the [[Ghorman Massacre]]. [[Wilmon Paak]] and [[Dreena]] also took shelter in the safehouse after fleeing the [[Ghorman Massacre]].<ref name="WTTR">{{Andor|Welcome to the Rebellion}}</ref>

In [[1 BBY]], the safehouse had been stripped bare, with several wall panels missing and the floor suffering from water damage. Following Rael's capture by [[Dedra Meero]], [[Kleya Marki]] retrieved a bag of equipment from a hidden compartment in the ceiling before setting off for [[Lina Soh Hospital]] to prevent Rael from being revived and subsequently interrogated by the [[Imperial Security Bureau|ISB]].<ref name="MIK">{{Andor|Make It Stop}}</ref>

Once her [[Infiltration of Lina Soh Hospital|mission]] was a success, Marki returned to the safehouse, where she broke open a wall to retrieve a [[fractal radio]] and plugged it into the building's power grid in order to send a coded distress signal to [[Yavin 4]] for immediate extraction. Her call was answered by Andor, who signaled back, unaware that the ISB, who had taken control of [[Galactic Antiquities and Objects of Interest]] was intercepting their communications, enabling [[ISB Supervisor]] [[Avril Heert]] to locate the safehouse.<ref name="WEK">{{Andor|Who Else Knows?}}</ref>

When Andor and [[Ruescott Melshi]] arrived at the safehouse, Marki informed them of Rael's death before desperately trying to recall all she knew of [[Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine]]'s [[Project Stardust|energy project]]. And argument ensued between Marki and Andor over Rael's decision to stay on Coruscant, especially with Marki reluctant to leave for Yavin. While they were distracted, Heert's [[ISB Tactical|Tactical]] team had arrived at [[Tomkip Towers]] and began triangulating the safehouse's position.<ref name="WEK" /> [[Raid on the Axis safehouse|A blaster fight]] soon broke out between the rebels and ISB, which soon ended when [[K-2SO]] ambushed the Imperials from behind. The rebels then departed the safehouse and fled Coruscant before Imperial reinforcements arrived.<ref name="Jedha">{{Andor|Jedha, Kyber, Erso}}</ref>

